{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"17 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,5.301,3.651,3.268,"ITC"],[13.889,14.731,31.393,2.373,2.124,"Priced for a full cigarette recovery"],[13.889,20.845,52.931,1.809,1.634,"ITC has lost 23% this year after dividends. On 1 February 2026 GST on"],[13.889,22.289,52.936,1.809,1.634,"cigarettes rose from 28% to 40% and excise duty jumped, on a business that"],[13.889,23.733,52.951,1.809,1.634,"earned 82% of FY26 segment profit. The shares are up 16% from October’s low,"],[13.889,25.177,52.934,1.809,1.634,"11% since Q2 FY27 results on 2 November. With the other businesses at peer"],[13.889,26.621,52.934,1.809,1.634,"multiples, ₹295 pays 14.6x forward cigarette earnings; eight listed tobacco peers"],[13.889,28.065,52.951,1.809,1.634,"trade at a median 13x. Even if cigarette profit regains its FY26 level by FY29E,"],[13.889,29.509,39.379,1.809,1.634,"our two methods average ₹292. Recovery is priced: Neutral."],[13.889,31.995,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Q2 FY27 showed two companies. Cigarette revenue net of excise fell 21% and"],[13.889,33.439,52.931,1.809,1.634,"segment profit 26% (Q1: 31%); ITC is passing the tax on in stages to limit the"],[13.889,34.883,52.934,1.809,1.634,"shift to smuggled brands, and profit rose 7% on Q1. Everything else grew. Other"],[13.889,36.328,52.992,1.809,1.634,"FMCG revenue rose 19% and profit 31%; paper profit rose 51% with Century"],[13.889,37.772,52.936,1.809,1.634,"Pulp and Paper (₹3,367 cr paid) in from 1 August; non-cigarette segment profit"],[13.889,39.216,52.954,1.809,1.634,"rose 23%. Group EBITDA still fell 16%. We assume cigarette profit rises 6-7%"],[13.889,40.684,52.931,1.809,1.634,"a quarter in H2, then 15% in FY28E and 8% in FY29E, to 93% of its FY26"],[13.889,42.128,37.234,1.809,1.634,"level. EPS falls 18% in FY27E, then grows 14% and 9%."],[13.889,44.59,52.936,1.809,1.634,"Our Dec-27 target of ₹280 averages a sum of parts (₹277) and a ten-year DCF at"],[13.889,46.034,52.966,1.809,1.634,"a 12% cost of equity plus cash and the ITC Hotels stake (₹283). The parts:"],[13.889,47.502,52.934,1.809,1.634,"cigarettes ₹145 at 13x; other FMCG ₹64 at 37.5x, the Indian consumer-peer"],[13.889,48.946,52.936,1.809,1.634,"median; agri and paper ₹27 at an assumed 15x; ITC Infotech ₹8, at its Happiest"],[13.889,50.39,52.959,1.809,1.634,"Minds merger value less 20%; ITC Hotels ₹9; cash ₹24. Consensus has FY28E"],[13.889,51.834,52.988,1.809,1.634,"EPS back at the FY26 level, a year before we do, and a mean target of ₹319. A"],[13.889,53.278,52.951,1.809,1.634,"4.2% dividend yield (FY27E ₹12.50, our assumption) limits the downside."],[13.889,54.722,52.959,1.809,1.634,"Risks: another duty rise in the February 2027 Budget; illicit trade, which ITC"],[13.889,56.167,41.401,1.809,1.634,"puts at a third of the legal market. Upside: price rises that stick."],[13.889,58.654,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[15.268,67.265,1.489,1.022,0.915,"250"],[15.268,64.904,1.489,1.022,0.915,"300"],[15.268,62.554,1.489,1.022,0.915,"350"],[15.268,60.195,1.489,1.022,0.915,"400"],[18.224,67.96,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.848,67.96,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.635,67.96,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.391,67.96,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[19.266,69.131,1.988,1.275,1.111,"ITC ("],[21.257,69.157,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[21.87,69.131,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[24.954,69.131,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.956,70.291,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.988,70.291,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[29.61,70.291,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,70.291,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,71.356,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.455,71.356,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−23.2%"],[24.517,71.356,2.811,1.387,1.209,"12.0%"],[28.691,71.356,2.26,1.387,1.209,"6.1%"],[32.945,71.356,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−24.2%"],[15.492,72.421,1.476,1.387,1.209,"Rel"],[19.455,72